WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.403
-You guys?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:06.105
You can feel it.
I can feel it.

00:00:06.105 --> 00:00:07.774
Spring is on the way.

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:09.042
The days are getting longer.

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:11.378
People are starting to make
their warm weather plans

00:00:11.378 --> 00:00:13.646
and that includes
my Monologue writers.

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:16.349
You know, they write hundreds of
jokes every day

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:18.851
just to get the 10 or 12 we end
up using in the Monologue.

00:00:18.851 --> 00:00:22.388
And honestly, a lot of those
jokes are not good.

00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:23.923
[ Laughter ]
It's just we're being honest.

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:25.758
This is an honest place.

00:00:25.758 --> 00:00:28.027
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.027 --> 00:00:31.363
And sometimes if we are
continuing to be honest,

00:00:31.363 --> 00:00:33.666
I think they throw in a few
stinkers just to

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:35.134
fill the page
and meet the assignment,

00:00:35.134 --> 00:00:36.703
but just because spring
is on the way

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.805
and birdsong is in the air,
doesn't mean you can

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:40.940
tolerate laziness.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:43.543
Which means it's time for
another Surprise Inspection.

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:46.879 line:85%
[ Fanfare plays ]

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:46.879
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.879 --> 00:00:50.349 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:50.349 --> 00:00:52.452
-And let me just say
I would put our writers

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:54.554
up against any other
writing staff in the world,

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:57.456
I think they are absolutely
A-plus joke writers,

00:00:57.456 --> 00:00:59.692
but you gotta --
I think the surprise inspection

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:02.961
is one of the things
that keeps them shipshape.

00:01:02.961 --> 00:01:03.996
So here's how this works,

00:01:03.996 --> 00:01:05.398
I'm going to read
some real jokes

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:07.633
submitted by my writers
that are unusable for the show.

00:01:07.633 --> 00:01:09.535
Some are dumb.
Some are offensive.

00:01:09.535 --> 00:01:10.770
Some are confusing.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.705
Most importantly,
most importantly,

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:14.106
the writers don't know
we're doing this

00:01:14.106 --> 00:01:16.108
and because a lot of them
don't watch the show,

00:01:16.108 --> 00:01:17.410
they'll never know.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.812
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.812 --> 00:01:21.414
So let's get started
with a real joke

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:24.050
that a real writer submitted.

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:26.518
Authorities in New Jersey
recently arrested

00:01:26.518 --> 00:01:30.222
an alleged burglar after they
matched his DNA to saliva

00:01:30.222 --> 00:01:33.092
that was found on the stairs
of the home he robbed.

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:37.297
And I'm just glad someone's
maintaining the drool of law.

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:39.965
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.965 --> 00:01:44.037
It's not -- it's too bad to even
be considered a dad joke.

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:47.707
It's like an absentee
father joke.

00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:50.376
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:53.579
Ian wrote it. Can we show Ian?
There you go.

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:56.148
That guy's just walking around
all cocky thinking like,

00:01:56.148 --> 00:01:57.383
"Yeah, I nailed it today."

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:59.752
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:02.488
A section of highway in --
a section of highway

00:02:02.488 --> 00:02:05.458
in Alabama was closed yesterday
after a truck,

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:08.962
hauling 45,000 pounds
of chicken fat, overturned.

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:13.099
Experts are calling it the most
horrific schmaltz disaster

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:15.568
since the "Donny and Marie" show
got canceled.

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:18.471
[ Light laughter, groans ]

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:21.240
So that joke relies on people
knowing that

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:24.643
chicken fat
is known as schmaltz.

00:02:24.643 --> 00:02:27.780
And then the next part of the
joke relies on people

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:30.849
thinking that "Donny and Marie"
like an act

00:02:30.849 --> 00:02:33.719
from like 40 years ago,
were schmaltzy,

00:02:33.719 --> 00:02:36.422
so it required
two things to work.

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:39.392
And even then, it doesn't.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:41.260
Brian wrote that joke.
Let's see, Brian.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.863
There you go.

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:48.034
Brian, Brian was born in the
heyday of "Donny and Marie."

00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:51.471
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.471 --> 00:02:54.440
An abandoned cargo ship
that contains more than

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:57.009
1000 luxury vehicles,
including Porsches,

00:02:57.009 --> 00:02:59.912
recently caught fire
off the coast of Portugal.

00:02:59.912 --> 00:03:04.283
Weird, I thought Lisbions
only drove Subarus.

00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:09.422
[ Groaning laughter,
light applause ]

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:14.260
I mean.
Yeah, okay.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.696
You know...

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:19.399
based on the first two,

00:03:19.399 --> 00:03:21.367
that one's definitely
in the top three.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:22.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.534 --> 00:03:23.903
Matt wrote that joke,
we should show him

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:25.938
since he got a smattering of
applause, yeah.

00:03:25.938 --> 00:03:27.674
Oh, don't.
Don't do it, guys.

00:03:30.943 --> 00:03:32.779
Alright.

00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:35.515
A dog in California
was recently reunited

00:03:35.515 --> 00:03:38.684
with its family after it
was missing for 12 years,

00:03:38.684 --> 00:03:42.889
though if you ask me,
that could be any dog in there.

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:47.227
[ Sad laughter ]

00:03:50.663 --> 00:03:52.165
Ali?

00:03:52.165 --> 00:03:54.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.768
See look -- yeah.

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:57.536
I heard Amber laugh,
Amber knows Ali,

00:03:57.536 --> 00:04:00.406
and she's not
surprised by that joke.

00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:02.342
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:04.543
Today was the first day of Lent,

00:04:04.543 --> 00:04:07.480
so ladies, right away,

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:10.216
I'm already terrified
that there's a "so ladies."

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:12.085
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:12.085 --> 00:04:13.886
Today was the first day of Lent,

00:04:13.886 --> 00:04:16.723
so ladies,
you best be giving it up.

00:04:24.696 --> 00:04:26.332
Colin's?
[ Laughs ]

00:04:30.769 --> 00:04:33.105
We got a, I think,
our first "boo."

00:04:33.105 --> 00:04:36.075
That was a, there was
an audible "boo" in there.

00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:37.743
Carnival Cruise Line
has announced

00:04:37.743 --> 00:04:39.979
that beginning next month,
it will make masks

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:42.715
optional for all guests
and offer more flexible

00:04:42.715 --> 00:04:44.316
pre-sailing
testing requirements.

00:04:44.316 --> 00:04:47.320
They'll also be launching
a new fleet.

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:50.857
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.857 --> 00:04:53.126
You guys, you guys remember
that dog joke.

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:54.827
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:57.263
You guys remember who wrote it?

00:04:57.263 --> 00:04:58.497
Well, guess what?

00:04:58.497 --> 00:05:04.737
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:07.907
They won't do my urn joke,
maybe they'll try casket.

00:05:07.907 --> 00:05:11.177
[ Laughter ]

00:05:11.177 --> 00:05:14.012
And finally, tomorrow
is National Grammar Day.

00:05:14.012 --> 00:05:16.381
"When isn't it?"
said White people.

00:05:16.448 --> 00:05:20.086
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:05:20.086 --> 00:05:21.887
It's a Kelsey Grammer joke,
everybody.

00:05:21.887 --> 00:05:24.123
Oh, yeah there's Colin.

00:05:24.123 --> 00:05:26.325
Ah, you guys, that has been,
this has been

00:05:26.325 --> 00:05:27.793
Surprise Inspection.

00:05:27.793 --> 00:05:33.232
[ Fanfare plays ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

